   "titulo": "Aula",
   "instrucao": "Clique em 🔊 para ouvir.",
   "html": "\n<p>Os possessivos indicam de quem é algo. Em francês eles concordam com <strong>a coisa possuída</strong>, não com quem possui.</p>\n<div class=\"tabela-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th></th><th>masc. sing.</th><th>fem. sing.</th><th>plural</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>je</td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"mon\">mon</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"ma\">ma</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"mes\">mes</span></td></tr><tr><td>tu</td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"ton\">ton</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"ta\">ta</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"tes\">tes</span></td></tr><tr><td>il / elle</td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"son\">son</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"sa\">sa</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"ses\">ses</span></td></tr><tr><td>nous</td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"notre\">notre</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"notre\">notre</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"nos\">nos</span></td></tr><tr><td>vous</td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"votre\">votre</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"votre\">votre</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"vos\">vos</span></td></tr><tr><td>ils / elles</td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"leur\">leur</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"leur\">leur</span></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"leurs\">leurs</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"destaque\"><strong>A armadilha:</strong> <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"son travail\">son travail</span> pode ser \"o trabalho dele\" ou \"o trabalho dela\". <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"Marie aime son travail.\">Marie aime son travail.</span> <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"Pierre aime son travail.\">Pierre aime son travail.</span> É SON nos dois casos, porque <em>travail</em> é masculino.</div>\n<h3>MON também serve para palavras femininas</h3>\n<p>Se a palavra feminina singular começar com <strong>vogal ou h mudo</strong>, usa-se mon/ton/son no lugar de ma/ta/sa, só pela pronúncia: <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"mon amie\">mon amie</span>, <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"ton histoire\">ton histoire</span>, <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"son école\">son école</span>.</p>\n<div class=\"tabela-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Feminina com vogal → MON</th><th>Feminina com consoante → MA</th><th>Masculina → MON</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une amie\">une amie</span> <small>uma amiga -&gt; mon amie</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une maison\">une maison</span> <small>uma casa -&gt; ma maison</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"un ami\">un ami</span> <small>um amigo -&gt; mon ami</small></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une histoire\">une histoire</span> <small>uma história -&gt; mon histoire</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une sœur\">une sœur</span> <small>uma irmã -&gt; ma sœur</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"un travail\">un travail</span> <small>um trabalho -&gt; mon travail</small></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une école\">une école</span> <small>uma escola -&gt; mon école</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une voiture\">une voiture</span> <small>um carro -&gt; ma voiture</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"un poste\">un poste</span> <small>um cargo -&gt; mon poste</small></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une adresse\">une adresse</span> <small>um endereço -&gt; mon adresse</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une formation\">une formation</span> <small>uma formação -&gt; ma formation</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"un frère\">un frère</span> <small>um irmão -&gt; mon frère</small></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une entreprise\">une entreprise</span> <small>uma empresa -&gt; mon entreprise</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une collègue\">une collègue</span> <small>uma colega -&gt; ma collègue</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"un collègue\">un collègue</span> <small>um colega -&gt; mon collègue</small></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une idée\">une idée</span> <small>uma ideia -&gt; mon idée</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une famille\">une famille</span> <small>uma família -&gt; ma famille</small></td><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"un entretien\">un entretien</span> <small>uma entrevista -&gt; mon entretien</small></td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"une équipe\">une équipe</span> <small>uma equipe -&gt; mon équipe</small></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<h3>Singular × plural</h3>\n<ul><li><strong>notre / votre / leur</strong> = um objeto: <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"notre maison\">notre maison</span>, <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"leur enfant\">leur enfant</span></li><li><strong>nos / vos / leurs</strong> = vários objetos: <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"nos maisons\">nos maisons</span>, <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"leurs enfants\">leurs enfants</span></li></ul>\n<h3>Monsieur, Madame, Mademoiselle</h3>\n<p>O possessivo já está dentro dessas palavras (mon + sieur, ma + dame): no plural, <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"Messieurs\">Messieurs</span>, <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"Mesdames\">Mesdames</span>, <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"Mesdemoiselles\">Mesdemoiselles</span>. Por isso <em>Notre-Dame</em> significa \"Nossa Senhora\".</p>\n<div class=\"dica\"><strong>Cuidado:</strong> <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"mon copain\">mon copain</span> (e às vezes <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"mon ami\">mon ami</span>) costuma soar como \"meu namorado\". Para \"um amigo meu\", diga <span class=\"fr\" data-fr=\"C'est un ami à moi.\">C'est un ami à moi.</span></div>"
  },
